# --- Google Sheets connection (primary PO data source) ---
# Read-only, via Google's public CSV export — confirmed acceptable as long
# as the sheet stays shared as "Anyone with the link can view". No service
# account/credentials needed.
#
# These values already point at the confirmed sheet and its Zepto/Blinkit/
# Instamart POs tabs + the EAN pricing tab. Copy this file to .env to use
# it as-is; only change it if the sheet or its tabs change.
GOOGLE_SHEET_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/14AATV91E-83_HL40TTbQA5NZtm_w9FQfXmrxgBKWDLM/edit

# Each tab's gid (the number after #gid= when you open that tab in the
# browser). BigBasket is intentionally not listed — out of v1 scope, see
# README.
GOOGLE_SHEET_GID_ZEPTO=710721210
GOOGLE_SHEET_GID_BLINKIT=1379386449
GOOGLE_SHEET_GID_INSTAMART=260331576

# Flipkart Minutes — column mapping confirmed (Status/PO number/PO
# IssueDate/Expiry Date/Scheduled Date/City/Location/Frido Dispatch WH/
# Total PO Qty/FSN — see TAB_CONFIG["Flipkart Minutes"] in
# src/lib/sheets/marketplaces.ts). The header row is auto-detected (its
# sheet has a merged title row above the real header, at no fixed
# offset), so only the gid is needed — same pattern as the other three,
# if it's a tab in this same workbook:
GOOGLE_SHEET_GID_FLIPKART_MINUTES=<gid>
#
# If Flipkart Minutes' data instead lives in its own separate workbook,
# set this too (falls back to GOOGLE_SHEET_URL above when unset):
# FLIPKART_MINUTES_SHEET_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<id>/edit

# "EAN" tab — used to look up each SKU's Cost Price to compute PO Value
# (PO Value isn't a column in the marketplace tabs themselves).
GOOGLE_SHEET_GID_EAN=1431578453

# --- Demand Intelligence (SKU-level sales data, separate workbook) ---
# A separate Google Sheet (confirmed: not additional tabs in the PO
# workbook) with one "Product Summary" tab: Platform, Category,
# Sub-Category, Master SKU, SKU ID, Product, GMV, Units, ASP, Spend,
# TACoS%. Also read via public CSV export — same sharing requirement as
# the PO sheet. "Master SKU" is the join key against each PO tab's "SKU"
# column (confirmed identical codes, e.g. FR-TNP-SB1, across both sheets).
SALES_SHEET_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/16N35WWf3shU6NFK_QyUQApvZPNJltJ0t/edit

# --- Supabase ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL is your project's URL (Project Settings → API).
# It's fine for this to be public — it's just an endpoint, not a credential.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY — the "service_role" secret key from Project
# Settings → API → Project API keys. NOT the anon/publishable key, and
# NOT prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ — this must never be exposed to the browser.
# Every table's Row Level Security now denies the anon role by default
# (see supabase/migrations/0014_lock_down_rls.sql), so the app's server
# code needs this key to read/write anything at all. Keep this out of
# version control (this file is committed as a template only — never put
# a real key here; set the real value in your local .env, which is
# gitignored, and in your hosting provider's env vars for production).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Automatic sync scheduler ---
# Protects /api/cron/sync from being triggered by anyone who finds the
# URL. Vercel Cron (see vercel.json) sends this automatically as a
# Bearer token when CRON_SECRET is set in the project's env vars; an
# external scheduler must send the same header. Leave unset only for
# local development — the route allows unauthenticated calls when this
# is blank, matching "no secret configured yet" rather than "misconfigured".
CRON_SECRET=
